  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below normal temperatures continue for the \nbeginning of the week before warming takes hold towards mid-late\nweek.\n\nAs low pressure moves into the Canadian Maritimes this weekend \nand high pressure builds to our west, northwesterly flow will \ncontinue to usher chilly air into the region. This will keep \ntemperatures slightly below normal for the start of the new \nweek. Clouds continue to wrap around, keeping temps elevated\nearly this morning, but this may not be the case in subsequent\nmornings, allowing for a bit more radiational cooling each\nsubsequent night for a few days. By contrast, highs will start\nto warm as cold advection dwindles and the sun becomes more\ndominant, so expect a widening of the diurnal range overall.\nWinds will remain a bit gusty today but should be diminished\ncompared to yesterday, and should diminish even more tomorrow as\ncompared to today. \n\nWhile the northwest flow may still allow a few\nsprinkles/flurries to reach the Poconos/NW NJ today, that should\nend tomorrow, with dry weather predominating the remainder of\nthe week.\n\nWarming of both highs and lows will commence by Wednesday and\ncontinue til week's end.",
